      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can achieve necessary transparency by politely acknowledging the condition of the packaging was reported but that your internal tracking data is clear regarding the safe journey to their address. Instead of directly accusing them, you can state you want to make things right despite the tracking, which frames the offer as an *act of service* rather than a *concession to fraud claim*. This approach addresses the facts while prioritizing the relationship, which is what ultimately deflects the need for a negative review.",
